    "9"
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "9"
  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals p x plus r\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></math> defines the line. In this equation, <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> represents the slope of the line and <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the line. It&rsquo;s given that the line has a slope of <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
